PATCH 484: the measurement chain 08e8 / a17e / a186 / a18e dropped their RETURN VALUE -- correct by
accident at -O0 (native), garbage at -O2 (wasm).

asm: 0x8e8 ends `mov [0x458],ax; mov [0x45a],dx; ret`, so AX (the 32-bit distance's LOW word, also stored
at DGROUP:0x458) is the result; 0xa17e / 0xa186 / 0xa18e are pure `call <target>; lret` forwarders whose
result is the callee's AX (08e8 range, 031c, 0578 bearing).  Ghidra emitted a bare `return;` in all four
non-void functions, so the value each caller received depended on what the compiler happened to leave in
the return register -- the same defect class as patch 481's e1d1/e132/e189 and the reason the AZER1
self-play still drifted native<->wasm after the object-level fixes: every range/bearing measurement in
the AI (target acquisition, aim, proximity) flowed through these four.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -5636,7 +5636,10 @@
   lVar3 = (uVar2 >> (uVar2 < uVar1)) + (uVar1 >> (uVar2 >= uVar1));
   DAT_1000_c458 = (int)lVar3;
   DAT_1000_c45a = (int)((ulong)lVar3 >> 0x10);
-  return;
+  /* PATCH 484: asm 0x8e8 ends `mov [0x458],ax; mov [0x45a],dx; ret` -- AX (the distance LOW word) is the
+   * return value and a17e/054c/9efc's callers consume it.  Ghidra emitted a bare `return;` in a non-void
+   * function: -O0 (native) happened to leave the right value in the return register, -O2 (wasm) did not. */
+  return (undefined4)(uint16_t)DAT_1000_c458;
 }
 
 
